{"stories": [{"title": "Validate WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility in all generated DOCX files", "priority": "high", "description": "Add accessibility validation to the DOCX generation pipeline. Check heading hierarchy (h1→h2→h3), table header rows, image alt text, and color contrast to ensure all generated IT-020 documents meet Malaysian government WCAG 2.1 AA standards required for JPK submission.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["Script: scripts/validate_docx_accessibility.py reads all output/*.docx files and checks WCAG 2.1 AA compliance using python-docx library (heading structure, table headers, alt text presence)", "Output: output/accessibility_audit.json lists violations per document with severity levels (critical/warning) and remediation guidance", "CLI: uv run scripts/validate_docx_accessibility.py exits with code 0 if all DOCX files are WCAG 2.1 AA compliant, code 1 if violations found; prints summary to stdout"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium", "_source": "product-owner"}, {"title": "Analyze learning activity distribution to ensure pedagogical diversity standards", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create analyzer that audits the balance of learning activities across each CoCu: practical labs, theoretical lectures, projects, and case studies. Flag units with excessive reliance on a single activity type (>70%) to improve pedagogical quality and meet NOSS competency-based learning standards.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["Script: scripts/analyze_activity_diversity.py parses content/IT-020-{3,4,5}/*.md and classifies all learning activities into: practical, theoretical, project, case_study using keyword matching", "Output: output/activity_distribution.csv with columns: CoCu_File, CoCu_Title, Practical%, Theoretical%, Project%, CaseStudy%, Diversity_Score, Flag", "CLI: uv run scripts/analyze_activity_diversity.py exits 0 if all units pass diversity threshold (no single type >70%), 1 if violations found; highlights low-diversity units for rebalancing"], "estimatedComplexity": "small", "_source": "product-owner"}, {"title": "Extract and validate learning progressions across L3→L4→L5 prerequisite chain", "priority": "medium", "description": "Build learning path validator that identifies prerequisite relationships: which L3 units enable L4 units, which L4 units enable L5 units. Validate that learning outcomes properly sequence from foundational (L3: Understand) to advanced (L5: Create/Evaluate) cognitive complexity per Bloom's taxonomy.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["Script: scripts/validate_learning_progressions.py analyzes learning outcomes, contact hours, and skill requirements across all 20 CoCu to build dependency graph using string similarity matching on learning outcome keywords", "Output: output/prerequisite_matrix.json showing dependencies (e.g., {L3_CoCu_1: [L4_CoCu_2, L4_CoCu_3]}) and output/progression_gaps.json listing any orphaned CoCu units or circular dependencies", "CLI: uv run scripts/validate_learning_progressions.py exits 0 if progressions are valid and sequential across levels, 1 if gaps/circular dependencies detected; recommends remediation"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium", "_source": "product-owner"}, {"title": "Generate trainer readiness assessment from competency extraction and instructor roster", "priority": "medium", "description": "Create assessment tool that cross-references extracted trainer competency requirements (hardware/software from all CoCu) against an instructor roster with existing certifications. Identify certification gaps and recommend optimal trainer-to-CoCu assignments.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["Script: scripts/generate_trainer_assessment.py reads output/trainer_competency_matrix.csv (generated by extract_trainer_competencies.py) and scripts/instructor_roster.csv (user-maintained: name, certifications, availability_hours)", "Output: output/trainer_readiness_gaps.json with columns: Technology, Required_By_CoCu, Certified_Instructors, Gaps, Recommended_Assignments and output/trainer_assignment_plan.csv", "CLI: uv run scripts/generate_trainer_assessment.py exits 0 if all CoCu can be covered by available instructors, 1 if gaps exist; suggests external training or hiring needs"], "estimatedComplexity": "small", "_source": "product-owner"}, {"title": "Create JPK audit report aggregating all compliance validations with submission readiness verdict", "priority": "high", "description": "Generate comprehensive JPK audit report that bundles all validation artifacts (checklists, K/P weighting reports, Bloom's taxonomy audits, accessibility audits, activity diversity analysis, progression validation, trainer readiness) into a single executive summary. Include submission readiness verdict and remediation checklist.", "acceptanceCriteria": ["Script: scripts/generate_jpk_audit_report.py aggregates output from all validation scripts (validate_kp_split.py, generate_jpk_checklist.py, validate_blooms_taxonomy.py, validate_docx_accessibility.py, analyze_activity_diversity.py, validate_learning_progressions.py, generate_trainer_assessment.py)", "Output: output/JPK_AUDIT_REPORT.md (human-readable executive summary with pass/fail status per validation category) and output/jpk_audit_manifest.json (structured with timestamps, file hashes, and audit evidence references)", "CLI: uv run scripts/generate_jpk_audit_report.py exits 0 if audit passes all mandatory validations and verdict is 'READY_FOR_JPK_SUBMISSION', 1 if critical gaps found; prints remediation checklist to stdout"], "estimatedComplexity": "medium", "_source": "product-owner"}]}
